{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XaPGNU3AB8Yu6pHDpw2dPP","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding. Let me create a detailed summary of the existing code patterns and architecture.\n\n## Comprehensive Code Pattern Summary\n\nBased on my exploration of the Ralph Wiggum V3 codebase, here's a detailed breakdown of the existing code patterns and structure:\n\n---\n\n## 1. WebSocket Message Handling Pattern (server/index.ts)\n\n### Architecture Overview\nThe server uses Express.js with a WebSocket server (ws library) for bidirectional communication. The `index.ts` file (436 lines) is the main server hub that orchestrates all services.\n\n### Key Patterns:\n\n**Connection Management:**\n- Maintains a `Set<WebSocket>` of connected clients\n- Broadcast function sends messages to all connected clients with `readyState` checking\n- Graceful cleanup on client disconnect\n\n```typescript\n// Pattern: Client tracking and broadcasting\nconst clients = new Set<WebSocket>();\nfunction broadcast(message: object) {\n  const data = JSON.stringify(message);\n  clients.forEach((client) => {\n    if (client.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {\n      client.send(data);\n    }\n  });\n}\n```\n\n**Message Handling Pattern:**\n- Type-based message routing using `switch` statements\n- Structured `type: 'action:subaction'` format for messages\n- Payload validation via JSON parsing with try-catch\n- Asynchronous message handling with `ws.on('message', async (data) => {})`\n\n**Message Types Follow Convention:**\n- `loop:*` - Loop execution control (start, stop, status, log)\n- `config:*` - Configuration file operations (read, write, refresh)\n- `agents:*` - Agent toggling and installation\n- `plan:*` - Plan generation workflow\n- `prd:*` - PRD document generation\n- `docs:*` - Document reading with path validation\n- `rules:*` - Cursor rules management\n- `claude:*` - CLAUDE.md file operations\n- `project:*` - Project scanning and info\n- `dependencies:*` - Dependency checking\n\n**Initial State Pattern:**\nWhen a client connects, the server sends initial state for all subsystems:\n```typescript\nws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'loop:status', payload: loopController.getStatus() }));\nws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'tasks:update', payload: fileWatcher.getTasks() }));\nws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'git:update', payload: fileWatcher.getGitStatus() }));\nws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'config:update', payload: projectConfig.getConfig() }));\nws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'project:info', payload: projectRoot }));\n```\n\n**Event Emitter Pattern:**\nAll services (FileWatcher, LoopController, PlanGenerator, PRDGenerator) extend EventEmitter and emit events that are broadcast to clients:\n```typescript\nfileWatcher.on('tasks', (tasks) => {\n  broadcast({ type: 'tasks:update', payload: tasks });\n});\n\nloopController.on('status', (status) => {\n  broadcast({ type: 'loop:status', payload: status });\n});\n\nplanGenerator.on('output', (text) => {\n  broadcast({ type: 'plan:output', payload: { text } });\n});\n```\n\n**Error Handling:**\n- Try-catch wraps message parsing\n- Errors logged to console and sometimes sent back to client\n- Graceful degradation (some operations fail silently)\n\n---\n\n## 2. Configuration Management (server/projectConfig.ts)\n\n### Architecture\nThe `ProjectConfigManager` class (653 lines) manages all project configuration with a dual-path system:\n- **ralphPath**: RalphWiggumV2's own directory (templates, prompts, agents)\n- **projectPath**: The target project being analyzed/modified\n\n### Key Patterns:\n\n**File Security Pattern:**\nAll file operations validate paths to prevent directory traversal:\n```typescript\nasync readFile(filename: string): Promise<string> {\n  if (filename.includes('..') || path.isAbsolute(filename)) {\n    throw new Error('Invalid filename');\n  }\n  const filePath = path.join(this.projectPath, filename);\n  return fs.readFile(filePath, 'utf-8');\n}\n```\n\n**Configuration State Pattern:**\nThe manager maintains a `ProjectConfig` object that caches file existence checks:\n```typescript\nthis.config = {\n  projectPath,\n  hasAgentsMd: checks[0],\n  hasClaudeMd,\n  hasImplementationPlan: checks[1],\n  hasPRD: checks[2],\n  hasAudienceJTBD: checks[3],\n  hasSpecs: checks[4],\n  hasCursorRules: checks[5],\n  hasLoopSh: checks[6],\n  enabledAgents: this.enabledAgents,\n};\n```\n\n**Refresh Pattern:**\nUses `Promise.all()` for parallel file existence checks:\n```typescript\nconst checks = await Promise.all([\n  this.fileExists('AGENTS.md'),\n  this.fileExists('IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md'),\n  // ... more checks\n]);\n```\n\n**Agent Parsing Pattern:**\nParses CLAUDE.md using regex to detect enabled agents:\n```typescript\nprivate async parseEnabledAgents(): Promise<string[]> {\n  const content = await this.readClaudeMd();\n  const enabled: string[] = [];\n  for (const agentId of ALL_AGENT_IDS) {\n    const disabledPattern = new RegExp(`<!-- DISABLED: ${agentId}[\\\\s\\\\S]*?-->`, 'g');\n    const enabledPattern = new RegExp(`\\`${agentId}\\``, 'g');\n    const contentWithoutDisabled = content.replace(disabledPattern, '');\n    if (enabledPattern.test(contentWithoutDisabled)) {\n      enabled.push(agentId);\n    }\n  }\n  return enabled;\n}\n```\n\n**Toggle Pattern:**\nAgent toggling uses comment wrapping for safe state management:\n```typescript\nif (enabled) {\n  // Remove DISABLED comments\n  const disabledPattern = new RegExp(`<!-- DISABLED: ${agentId}\\\\n([\\\\s\\\\S]*?)-->\\\\n?`, 'g');\n  content = content.replace(disabledPattern, '$1');\n} else {\n  // Wrap in DISABLED comments\n  content = this.disableAgentInContent(content, agentId);\n}\n```\n\n**Agent Installation Pattern:**\nAgents are copied from Ralph's repo to either:\n- Global: `~/.claude/agents/`\n- Project: `./.claude/agents/`\n\n```typescript\nasync installAgentGlobal(agentId: string): Promise<void> {\n  const sourcePath = path.join(this.ralphPath, '.claude', 'agents', `${agentId}.md`);\n  const globalDir = path.join(os.homedir(), '.claude', 'agents');\n  const destPath = path.join(globalDir, `${agentId}.md`);\n  \n  const content = await fs.readFile(sourcePath, 'utf-8');\n  await fs.mkdir(globalDir, { recursive: true });\n  await fs.writeFile(destPath, content, 'utf-8');\n}\n```\n\n**Cursor Rules Management:**\nRules can be enabled/disabled by renaming `.mdc` ↔ `.mdc.disabled`:\n```typescript\nif (enabled) {\n  await fs.rename(disabledPath, enabledPath);\n} else {\n  await fs.rename(enabledPath, disabledPath);\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Type System (src/types/index.ts)\n\n### Architecture\nComprehensive union-typed message system with strict separation of:\n- Server messages (broadcast from server)\n- Client commands (sent from client to server)\n- Domain-specific types (Loop, Tasks, Git, etc.)\n\n### Key Patterns:\n\n**Typed Message Pattern:**\nEach message type has both a broad interface and specific typed interface:\n```typescript\nexport interface WSMessage {\n  type: string;\n  payload: unknown;\n}\n\nexport interface LoopStatusMessage extends WSMessage {\n  type: 'loop:status';\n  payload: LoopStatus;\n}\n```\n\n**Union Types for Type Safety:**\n```typescript\nexport type ServerMessage =\n  | LoopStatusMessage\n  | LogMessage\n  | TasksMessage\n  | GitMessage\n  | ConfigMessage\n  | PlanStatusMessage\n  | PlanCompleteMessage\n  // ... more types\n```\n\n**Status Types Pattern:**\nAll async operations have dedicated status types:\n```typescript\nexport interface PlanGeneratorStatus {\n  generating: boolean;\n  mode: 'plan' | 'plan-slc' | 'plan-work' | null;\n  startedAt: Date | null;\n}\n\nexport interface PRDGeneratorStatus {\n  generating: boolean;\n  startedAt: Date | null;\n}\n```\n\n**Detailed Information Types:**\nDynamic information from the filesystem:\n```typescript\nexport interface AgentInfo {\n  id: string;\n  name: string;\n  description: string;\n  source: 'global' | 'project';\n  enabled: boolean;\n  filePath: string;\n}\n\nexport interface CursorRuleInfo {\n  id: string;\n  name: string;\n  description: string;\n  globs: string[];\n  enabled: boolean;\n  filePath: string;\n}\n```\n\n**Project Discovery Types:**\nSophisticated scanning output types:\n```typescript\nexport interface ProjectScan {\n  projectName: string;\n  projectPath: string;\n  scanMode: 'embedded' | 'standalone';\n  packageManager: 'npm' | 'yarn' | 'pnpm' | 'bun' | null;\n  framework: string | null;\n  language: 'typescript' | 'javascript' | 'python' | 'go' | 'mixed' | 'unknown';\n  detectedCommands: { build?: string; dev?: string; test?: string; /* ... */ };\n  allMarkdownFiles: DiscoveredDoc[];\n  hasRalphConfig: { /* ... */ };\n  subprojects: SubProject[];\n  isMonorepo: boolean;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Hook Pattern (src/hooks/useWebSocket.ts)\n\n### Architecture\nA comprehensive custom React hook managing all WebSocket state and communication. 590 lines of well-structured state management.\n\n### Key Patterns:\n\n**Ref-Based Connection Management:**\n```typescript\nconst wsRef = useRef<WebSocket | null>(null);\nconst reconnectTimeoutRef = useRef<ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | null>(null);\nconst isCleaningUpRef = useRef(false);\n```\n\n**Auto-Reconnect with Cleanup Safety:**\n```typescript\nws.onclose = () => {\n  if (!isCleaningUpRef.current) {\n    setConnected(false);\n    reconnectTimeoutRef.current = setTimeout(() => {\n      if (!isCleaningUpRef.current) {\n        connect();\n      }\n    }, 2000);\n  }\n};\n```\n\n**Cleanup Pattern to Prevent Memory Leaks:**\n```typescript\nreturn () => {\n  isCleaningUpRef.current = true;\n  if (reconnectTimeoutRef.current) {\n    clearTimeout(reconnectTimeoutRef.current);\n    reconnectTimeoutRef.current = null;\n  }\n  if (wsRef.current) {\n    wsRef.current.onerror = null;\n    wsRef.current.onclose = null;\n    wsRef.current.close();\n    wsRef.current = null;\n  }\n};\n```\n\n**Comprehensive State Management:**\nThe hook manages 40+ state variables organized by domain:\n```typescript\n// Loop/Build state\nconst [loopStatus, setLoopStatus] = useState<LoopStatus>(DEFAULT_LOOP_STATUS);\nconst [tasks, setTasks] = useState<TasksState>(DEFAULT_TASKS);\nconst [gitStatus, setGitStatus] = useState<GitStatus>(DEFAULT_GIT_STATUS);\nconst [logs, setLogs] = useState<LogEntry[]>([]);\n\n// Plan generation state\nconst [planStatus, setPlanStatus] = useState<PlanGeneratorStatus>(DEFAULT_PLAN_STATUS);\nconst [planOutput, setPlanOutput] = useState('');\nconst [planComplete, setPlanComplete] = useState<{ plan: string; output: string } | null>(null);\nconst [planError, setPlanError] = useState<string | null>(null);\n\n// Document selection and preview\nconst [selectedDocPaths, setSelectedDocPaths] = useState<string[]>([]);\nconst [previewDoc, setPreviewDoc] = useState<{ path: string; content: string } | null>(null);\nconst [isLoadingPreview, setIsLoadingPreview] = useState(false);\n\n// ... more state for PRD, agents, rules, CLAUDE.md, dependencies, etc.\n```\n\n**Message Dispatch Pattern:**\nAll server messages routed through a massive switch statement:\n```typescript\nswitch (message.type) {\n  case 'loop:status':\n    setLoopStatus(message.payload);\n    break;\n  case 'loop:log':\n    setLogs((prev) => [...prev.slice(-500), message.payload]); // Keep last 500\n    break;\n  case 'tasks:update':\n    setTasks(message.payload);\n    break;\n  // ... 30+ more cases\n}\n```\n\n**Log Management with Size Limit:**\n```typescript\ncase 'loop:log':\n  setLogs((prev) => [...prev.slice(-500), message.payload]); // Keep last 500\n  break;\n```\n\n**Output Streaming Pattern:**\n```typescript\ncase 'plan:output':\n  setPlanOutput((prev) => prev + message.payload.text);\n  break;\n```\n\n**State Clearing on Start:**\n```typescript\ncase 'plan:status':\n  setPlanStatus(message.payload);\n  if (message.payload.generating) {\n    // Clear previous results when starting new generation\n    setPlanOutput('');\n    setPlanComplete(null);\n    setPlanError(null);\n  }\n  break;\n```\n\n**Command Sending Pattern:**\n```typescript\nconst sendCommand = useCallback((command: ClientCommand) => {\n  if (wsRef.current?.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {\n    wsRef.current.send(JSON.stringify(command));\n  }\n}, []);\n```\n\n**Feature-Specific Handler Functions:**\nEach major feature has dedicated callbacks:\n```typescript\nconst scanProject = useCallback(() => {\n  if (wsRef.current?.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {\n    setScanLoading(true);\n    wsRef.current.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'project:scan' }));\n  }\n}, []);\n\nconst listAgents = useCallback(() => {\n  if (wsRef.current?.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {\n    setAgentsLoading(true);\n    wsRef.current.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'agents:list' }));\n  }\n}, []);\n\nconst readDoc = useCallback((docPath: string) => {\n  if (wsRef.current?.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {\n    setIsLoadingPreview(true);\n    setPreviewDoc(null);\n    wsRef.current.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'docs:read', payload: { docPath } }));\n  }\n}, []);\n```\n\n**Environment-Based Configuration:**\n```typescript\nconst DEFAULT_WS_PORT = import.meta.env.VITE_WS_PORT || '3001';\n\nexport function useWebSocket(url: string = `ws://localhost:${DEFAULT_WS_PORT}/ws`): UseWebSocketReturn {\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Supporting Services Architecture\n\n### FileWatcher (fileWatcher.ts - 314 lines)\n- Uses `chokidar` for file system monitoring\n- Watches multiple files: IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, ralph.log, PRD.md, AUDIENCE_JTBD.md, progress.txt, tasks.json\n- Emits events: `tasks`, `log`, `git`, `config:refresh`\n- Maintains git status with periodic updates (10-second intervals)\n- Tail-logs ralph.log for new entries only\n\n### LoopController (loopController.ts - 218 lines)\n- Spawns bash subprocess to execute loop.sh\n- Handles Windows/Linux bash detection\n- Manages loop modes: `plan`, `plan-slc`, `plan-work`, `build`\n- Emits status and log events\n- Tracks iteration count and process state\n\n### PlanGenerator & PRDGenerator\n- Similar event emitter pattern\n- Spawn subprocess for LLM-based generation\n- Emit streaming output as `output` events\n- Handle cancellation\n\n---\n\n## 6. Cross-Cutting Patterns\n\n### Security Patterns\n1. **Path validation**: Check for `..` and absolute paths\n2. **Safe file operations**: Use `fs/promises` with error handling\n3. **WebSocket connection state**: Always check `readyState === WebSocket.OPEN` before sending\n\n### Error Handling Patterns\n1. **Try-catch with logging**: Errors logged to console, sometimes sent to client\n2. **User-facing errors**: Specific error messages in WebSocket payload\n3. **Graceful degradation**: Missing files/directories don't crash the server\n\n### State Management Patterns\n1. **Immutable updates**: `setLogs((prev) => [...prev, newLog])`\n2. **Dual state tracking**: Loading states paired with data states\n3. **Event-driven updates**: Server pushes updates via events, client pulls via commands\n\n### Cleanup Patterns\n1. **Ref-based flags**: `isCleaningUpRef.current` prevents state updates during cleanup\n2. **Timeout clearing**: All timers cleared in cleanup\n3. **Event listener removal**: Explicitly set to null before closing connections\n\n---\n\n## 7. File Organization\n\n```\ndashboard/\n├── server/\n│   ├── index.ts                (436 lines) - Main WebSocket server & routing\n│   ├── projectConfig.ts        (653 lines) - Configuration management\n│   ├── fileWatcher.ts          (314 lines) - File system monitoring\n│   ├── loopController.ts       (218 lines) - Loop execution\n│   ├── planGenerator.ts        (289 lines) - Plan generation\n│   ├── prdGenerator.ts         (361 lines) - PRD generation\n│   ├── projectScanner.ts       (719 lines) - Project discovery\n│   ├── projectRootDetector.ts  (172 lines) - Root detection logic\n│   └── dependencyChecker.ts    (147 lines) - Tool availability checking\n│\n└── src/\n    ├── hooks/\n    │   └── useWebSocket.ts     (590 lines) - Main client hook\n    ├── types/\n    │   └── index.ts            (609 lines) - All type definitions\n    └── components/\n        ├── Dashboard.tsx\n        ├── LoopControls.tsx\n        ├── PlanGenerator.tsx\n        ├── PRDGenerator.tsx\n        └── ... (other UI components)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Key Conventions\n\n1. **Message Type Naming**: `domain:action` format (e.g., `loop:start`, `config:read`)\n2. **Service Instantiation**: All services initialized in index.ts with proper paths\n3. **Payload Wrapping**: All messages use `{ type: string, payload: unknown }`\n4. **Event Emission**: All async operations emit events for real-time UI updates\n5. **Error Objects**: Error strings in payload, not thrown objects\n6. **State Defaults**: Large DEFAULT_* constants at hook top for test isolation\n7. **Type Safety**: Full TypeScript with union types for message discrimination\n\n---\n\nThis is a production-quality, well-architected system that demonstrates:\n- Robust WebSocket communication patterns\n- Comprehensive type safety\n- Event-driven architecture\n- Proper error handling and cleanup\n- Security-conscious file operations\n- Scalable service layer design"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ae49d67 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d9df9ce-f430-4def-aa62-de4fb0297909","uuid":"fc9299f8-5ccf-4d5b-b564-f377695ce825","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the server directory to understand the existing code patterns. Focus on:\n1. How server/index.ts handles WebSocket messages\n2. How server/projectConfig.ts manages configuration\n3. What types exist in src/types/index.ts\n4. What patterns are used in existing hooks like useWebSocket.ts\n\nProvide a comprehensive summary of the existing patterns and code structure.","agentId":"ae49d67","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding. Let me create a detailed summary of the existing code patterns and architecture.\n\n## Comprehensive Code Pattern Summary\n\nBased on my exploration of the Ralph Wiggum V3 codebase, here's a detailed breakdown of the existing code patterns and structure:\n\n---\n\n## 1. WebSocket Message Handling Pattern (server/index.ts)\n\n### Architecture Overview\nThe server uses Express.js with a WebSocket server (ws library) for bidirectional communication. The `index.ts` file (436 lines) is the main server hub that orchestrates all services.\n\n### Key Patterns:\n\n**Connection Management:**\n- Maintains a `Set<WebSocket>` of connected clients\n- Broadcast function sends messages to all connected clients with `readyState` checking\n- Graceful cleanup on client disconnect\n\n```typescript\n// Pattern: Client tracking and broadcasting\nconst clients = new Set<WebSocket>();\nfunction broadcast(message: object) {\n  const data = JSON.stringify(message);\n  clients.forEach((client) => {\n    if (client.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {\n      client.send(data);\n    }\n  });\n}\n```\n\n**Message Handling Pattern:**\n- Type-based message routing using `switch` statements\n- Structured `type: 'action:subaction'` format for messages\n- Payload validation via JSON parsing with try-catch\n- Asynchronous message handling with `ws.on('message', async (data) => {})`\n\n**Message Types Follow Convention:**\n- `loop:*` - Loop execution control (start, stop, status, log)\n- `config:*` - Configuration file operations (read, write, refresh)\n- `agents:*` - Agent toggling and installation\n- `plan:*` - Plan generation workflow\n- `prd:*` - PRD document generation\n- `docs:*` - Document reading with path validation\n- `rules:*` - Cursor rules management\n- `claude:*` - CLAUDE.md file operations\n- `project:*` - Project scanning and info\n- `dependencies:*` - Dependency checking\n\n**Initial State Pattern:**\nWhen a client connects, the server sends initial state for all subsystems:\n```typescript\nws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'loop:status', payload: loopController.getStatus() }));\nws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'tasks:update', payload: fileWatcher.getTasks() }));\nws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'git:update', payload: fileWatcher.getGitStatus() }));\nws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'config:update', payload: projectConfig.getConfig() }));\nws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'project:info', payload: projectRoot }));\n```\n\n**Event Emitter Pattern:**\nAll services (FileWatcher, LoopController, PlanGenerator, PRDGenerator) extend EventEmitter and emit events that are broadcast to clients:\n```typescript\nfileWatcher.on('tasks', (tasks) => {\n  broadcast({ type: 'tasks:update', payload: tasks });\n});\n\nloopController.on('status', (status) => {\n  broadcast({ type: 'loop:status', payload: status });\n});\n\nplanGenerator.on('output', (text) => {\n  broadcast({ type: 'plan:output', payload: { text } });\n});\n```\n\n**Error Handling:**\n- Try-catch wraps message parsing\n- Errors logged to console and sometimes sent back to client\n- Graceful degradation (some operations fail silently)\n\n---\n\n## 2. Configuration Management (server/projectConfig.ts)\n\n### Architecture\nThe `ProjectConfigManager` class (653 lines) manages all project configuration with a dual-path system:\n- **ralphPath**: RalphWiggumV2's own directory (templates, prompts, agents)\n- **projectPath**: The target project being analyzed/modified\n\n### Key Patterns:\n\n**File Security Pattern:**\nAll file operations validate paths to prevent directory traversal:\n```typescript\nasync readFile(filename: string): Promise<string> {\n  if (filename.includes('..') || path.isAbsolute(filename)) {\n    throw new Error('Invalid filename');\n  }\n  const filePath = path.join(this.projectPath, filename);\n  return fs.readFile(filePath, 'utf-8');\n}\n```\n\n**Configuration State Pattern:**\nThe manager maintains a `ProjectConfig` object that caches file existence checks:\n```typescript\nthis.config = {\n  projectPath,\n  hasAgentsMd: checks[0],\n  hasClaudeMd,\n  hasImplementationPlan: checks[1],\n  hasPRD: checks[2],\n  hasAudienceJTBD: checks[3],\n  hasSpecs: checks[4],\n  hasCursorRules: checks[5],\n  hasLoopSh: checks[6],\n  enabledAgents: this.enabledAgents,\n};\n```\n\n**Refresh Pattern:**\nUses `Promise.all()` for parallel file existence checks:\n```typescript\nconst checks = await Promise.all([\n  this.fileExists('AGENTS.md'),\n  this.fileExists('IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md'),\n  // ... more checks\n]);\n```\n\n**Agent Parsing Pattern:**\nParses CLAUDE.md using regex to detect enabled agents:\n```typescript\nprivate async parseEnabledAgents(): Promise<string[]> {\n  const content = await this.readClaudeMd();\n  const enabled: string[] = [];\n  for (const agentId of ALL_AGENT_IDS) {\n    const disabledPattern = new RegExp(`<!-- DISABLED: ${agentId}[\\\\s\\\\S]*?-->`, 'g');\n    const enabledPattern = new RegExp(`\\`${agentId}\\``, 'g');\n    const contentWithoutDisabled = content.replace(disabledPattern, '');\n    if (enabledPattern.test(contentWithoutDisabled)) {\n      enabled.push(agentId);\n    }\n  }\n  return enabled;\n}\n```\n\n**Toggle Pattern:**\nAgent toggling uses comment wrapping for safe state management:\n```typescript\nif (enabled) {\n  // Remove DISABLED comments\n  const disabledPattern = new RegExp(`<!-- DISABLED: ${agentId}\\\\n([\\\\s\\\\S]*?)-->\\\\n?`, 'g');\n  content = content.replace(disabledPattern, '$1');\n} else {\n  // Wrap in DISABLED comments\n  content = this.disableAgentInContent(content, agentId);\n}\n```\n\n**Agent Installation Pattern:**\nAgents are copied from Ralph's repo to either:\n- Global: `~/.claude/agents/`\n- Project: `./.claude/agents/`\n\n```typescript\nasync installAgentGlobal(agentId: string): Promise<void> {\n  const sourcePath = path.join(this.ralphPath, '.claude', 'agents', `${agentId}.md`);\n  const globalDir = path.join(os.homedir(), '.claude', 'agents');\n  const destPath = path.join(globalDir, `${agentId}.md`);\n  \n  const content = await fs.readFile(sourcePath, 'utf-8');\n  await fs.mkdir(globalDir, { recursive: true });\n  await fs.writeFile(destPath, content, 'utf-8');\n}\n```\n\n**Cursor Rules Management:**\nRules can be enabled/disabled by renaming `.mdc` ↔ `.mdc.disabled`:\n```typescript\nif (enabled) {\n  await fs.rename(disabledPath, enabledPath);\n} else {\n  await fs.rename(enabledPath, disabledPath);\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Type System (src/types/index.ts)\n\n### Architecture\nComprehensive union-typed message system with strict separation of:\n- Server messages (broadcast from server)\n- Client commands (sent from client to server)\n- Domain-specific types (Loop, Tasks, Git, etc.)\n\n### Key Patterns:\n\n**Typed Message Pattern:**\nEach message type has both a broad interface and specific typed interface:\n```typescript\nexport interface WSMessage {\n  type: string;\n  payload: unknown;\n}\n\nexport interface LoopStatusMessage extends WSMessage {\n  type: 'loop:status';\n  payload: LoopStatus;\n}\n```\n\n**Union Types for Type Safety:**\n```typescript\nexport type ServerMessage =\n  | LoopStatusMessage\n  | LogMessage\n  | TasksMessage\n  | GitMessage\n  | ConfigMessage\n  | PlanStatusMessage\n  | PlanCompleteMessage\n  // ... more types\n```\n\n**Status Types Pattern:**\nAll async operations have dedicated status types:\n```typescript\nexport interface PlanGeneratorStatus {\n  generating: boolean;\n  mode: 'plan' | 'plan-slc' | 'plan-work' | null;\n  startedAt: Date | null;\n}\n\nexport interface PRDGeneratorStatus {\n  generating: boolean;\n  startedAt: Date | null;\n}\n```\n\n**Detailed Information Types:**\nDynamic information from the filesystem:\n```typescript\nexport interface AgentInfo {\n  id: string;\n  name: string;\n  description: string;\n  source: 'global' | 'project';\n  enabled: boolean;\n  filePath: string;\n}\n\nexport interface CursorRuleInfo {\n  id: string;\n  name: string;\n  description: string;\n  globs: string[];\n  enabled: boolean;\n  filePath: string;\n}\n```\n\n**Project Discovery Types:**\nSophisticated scanning output types:\n```typescript\nexport interface ProjectScan {\n  projectName: string;\n  projectPath: string;\n  scanMode: 'embedded' | 'standalone';\n  packageManager: 'npm' | 'yarn' | 'pnpm' | 'bun' | null;\n  framework: string | null;\n  language: 'typescript' | 'javascript' | 'python' | 'go' | 'mixed' | 'unknown';\n  detectedCommands: { build?: string; dev?: string; test?: string; /* ... */ };\n  allMarkdownFiles: DiscoveredDoc[];\n  hasRalphConfig: { /* ... */ };\n  subprojects: SubProject[];\n  isMonorepo: boolean;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Hook Pattern (src/hooks/useWebSocket.ts)\n\n### Architecture\nA comprehensive custom React hook managing all WebSocket state and communication. 590 lines of well-structured state management.\n\n### Key Patterns:\n\n**Ref-Based Connection Management:**\n```typescript\nconst wsRef = useRef<WebSocket | null>(null);\nconst reconnectTimeoutRef = useRef<ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | null>(null);\nconst isCleaningUpRef = useRef(false);\n```\n\n**Auto-Reconnect with Cleanup Safety:**\n```typescript\nws.onclose = () => {\n  if (!isCleaningUpRef.current) {\n    setConnected(false);\n    reconnectTimeoutRef.current = setTimeout(() => {\n      if (!isCleaningUpRef.current) {\n        connect();\n      }\n    }, 2000);\n  }\n};\n```\n\n**Cleanup Pattern to Prevent Memory Leaks:**\n```typescript\nreturn () => {\n  isCleaningUpRef.current = true;\n  if (reconnectTimeoutRef.current) {\n    clearTimeout(reconnectTimeoutRef.current);\n    reconnectTimeoutRef.current = null;\n  }\n  if (wsRef.current) {\n    wsRef.current.onerror = null;\n    wsRef.current.onclose = null;\n    wsRef.current.close();\n    wsRef.current = null;\n  }\n};\n```\n\n**Comprehensive State Management:**\nThe hook manages 40+ state variables organized by domain:\n```typescript\n// Loop/Build state\nconst [loopStatus, setLoopStatus] = useState<LoopStatus>(DEFAULT_LOOP_STATUS);\nconst [tasks, setTasks] = useState<TasksState>(DEFAULT_TASKS);\nconst [gitStatus, setGitStatus] = useState<GitStatus>(DEFAULT_GIT_STATUS);\nconst [logs, setLogs] = useState<LogEntry[]>([]);\n\n// Plan generation state\nconst [planStatus, setPlanStatus] = useState<PlanGeneratorStatus>(DEFAULT_PLAN_STATUS);\nconst [planOutput, setPlanOutput] = useState('');\nconst [planComplete, setPlanComplete] = useState<{ plan: string; output: string } | null>(null);\nconst [planError, setPlanError] = useState<string | null>(null);\n\n// Document selection and preview\nconst [selectedDocPaths, setSelectedDocPaths] = useState<string[]>([]);\nconst [previewDoc, setPreviewDoc] = useState<{ path: string; content: string } | null>(null);\nconst [isLoadingPreview, setIsLoadingPreview] = useState(false);\n\n// ... more state for PRD, agents, rules, CLAUDE.md, dependencies, etc.\n```\n\n**Message Dispatch Pattern:**\nAll server messages routed through a massive switch statement:\n```typescript\nswitch (message.type) {\n  case 'loop:status':\n    setLoopStatus(message.payload);\n    break;\n  case 'loop:log':\n    setLogs((prev) => [...prev.slice(-500), message.payload]); // Keep last 500\n    break;\n  case 'tasks:update':\n    setTasks(message.payload);\n    break;\n  // ... 30+ more cases\n}\n```\n\n**Log Management with Size Limit:**\n```typescript\ncase 'loop:log':\n  setLogs((prev) => [...prev.slice(-500), message.payload]); // Keep last 500\n  break;\n```\n\n**Output Streaming Pattern:**\n```typescript\ncase 'plan:output':\n  setPlanOutput((prev) => prev + message.payload.text);\n  break;\n```\n\n**State Clearing on Start:**\n```typescript\ncase 'plan:status':\n  setPlanStatus(message.payload);\n  if (message.payload.generating) {\n    // Clear previous results when starting new generation\n    setPlanOutput('');\n    setPlanComplete(null);\n    setPlanError(null);\n  }\n  break;\n```\n\n**Command Sending Pattern:**\n```typescript\nconst sendCommand = useCallback((command: ClientCommand) => {\n  if (wsRef.current?.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {\n    wsRef.current.send(JSON.stringify(command));\n  }\n}, []);\n```\n\n**Feature-Specific Handler Functions:**\nEach major feature has dedicated callbacks:\n```typescript\nconst scanProject = useCallback(() => {\n  if (wsRef.current?.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {\n    setScanLoading(true);\n    wsRef.current.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'project:scan' }));\n  }\n}, []);\n\nconst listAgents = useCallback(() => {\n  if (wsRef.current?.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {\n    setAgentsLoading(true);\n    wsRef.current.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'agents:list' }));\n  }\n}, []);\n\nconst readDoc = useCallback((docPath: string) => {\n  if (wsRef.current?.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {\n    setIsLoadingPreview(true);\n    setPreviewDoc(null);\n    wsRef.current.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'docs:read', payload: { docPath } }));\n  }\n}, []);\n```\n\n**Environment-Based Configuration:**\n```typescript\nconst DEFAULT_WS_PORT = import.meta.env.VITE_WS_PORT || '3001';\n\nexport function useWebSocket(url: string = `ws://localhost:${DEFAULT_WS_PORT}/ws`): UseWebSocketReturn {\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Supporting Services Architecture\n\n### FileWatcher (fileWatcher.ts - 314 lines)\n- Uses `chokidar` for file system monitoring\n- Watches multiple files: IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, ralph.log, PRD.md, AUDIENCE_JTBD.md, progress.txt, tasks.json\n- Emits events: `tasks`, `log`, `git`, `config:refresh`\n- Maintains git status with periodic updates (10-second intervals)\n- Tail-logs ralph.log for new entries only\n\n### LoopController (loopController.ts - 218 lines)\n- Spawns bash subprocess to execute loop.sh\n- Handles Windows/Linux bash detection\n- Manages loop modes: `plan`, `plan-slc`, `plan-work`, `build`\n- Emits status and log events\n- Tracks iteration count and process state\n\n### PlanGenerator & PRDGenerator\n- Similar event emitter pattern\n- Spawn subprocess for LLM-based generation\n- Emit streaming output as `output` events\n- Handle cancellation\n\n---\n\n## 6. Cross-Cutting Patterns\n\n### Security Patterns\n1. **Path validation**: Check for `..` and absolute paths\n2. **Safe file operations**: Use `fs/promises` with error handling\n3. **WebSocket connection state**: Always check `readyState === WebSocket.OPEN` before sending\n\n### Error Handling Patterns\n1. **Try-catch with logging**: Errors logged to console, sometimes sent to client\n2. **User-facing errors**: Specific error messages in WebSocket payload\n3. **Graceful degradation**: Missing files/directories don't crash the server\n\n### State Management Patterns\n1. **Immutable updates**: `setLogs((prev) => [...prev, newLog])`\n2. **Dual state tracking**: Loading states paired with data states\n3. **Event-driven updates**: Server pushes updates via events, client pulls via commands\n\n### Cleanup Patterns\n1. **Ref-based flags**: `isCleaningUpRef.current` prevents state updates during cleanup\n2. **Timeout clearing**: All timers cleared in cleanup\n3. **Event listener removal**: Explicitly set to null before closing connections\n\n---\n\n## 7. File Organization\n\n```\ndashboard/\n├── server/\n│   ├── index.ts                (436 lines) - Main WebSocket server & routing\n│   ├── projectConfig.ts        (653 lines) - Configuration management\n│   ├── fileWatcher.ts          (314 lines) - File system monitoring\n│   ├── loopController.ts       (218 lines) - Loop execution\n│   ├── planGenerator.ts        (289 lines) - Plan generation\n│   ├── prdGenerator.ts         (361 lines) - PRD generation\n│   ├── projectScanner.ts       (719 lines) - Project discovery\n│   ├── projectRootDetector.ts  (172 lines) - Root detection logic\n│   └── dependencyChecker.ts    (147 lines) - Tool availability checking\n│\n└── src/\n    ├── hooks/\n    │   └── useWebSocket.ts     (590 lines) - Main client hook\n    ├── types/\n    │   └── index.ts            (609 lines) - All type definitions\n    └── components/\n        ├── Dashboard.tsx\n        ├── LoopControls.tsx\n        ├── PlanGenerator.tsx\n        ├── PRDGenerator.tsx\n        └── ... (other UI components)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Key Conventions\n\n1. **Message Type Naming**: `domain:action` format (e.g., `loop:start`, `config:read`)\n2. **Service Instantiation**: All services initialized in index.ts with proper paths\n3. **Payload Wrapping**: All messages use `{ type: string, payload: unknown }`\n4. **Event Emission**: All async operations emit events for real-time UI updates\n5. **Error Objects**: Error strings in payload, not thrown objects\n6. **State Defaults**: Large DEFAULT_* constants at hook top for test isolation\n7. **Type Safety**: Full TypeScript with union types for message discrimination\n\n---\n\nThis is a production-quality, well-architected system that demonstrates:\n- Robust WebSocket communication patterns\n- Comprehensive type safety\n- Event-driven architecture\n- Proper error handling and cleanup\n- Security-conscious file operations\n- Scalable service layer design"}],"totalDurationMs":100817,"totalTokens":59162,"totalToolUseCount":23,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":650,"cache_read_input_tokens":53599,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":650,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4913,"service_tier":"standard"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UL2WkT46SPJU2cfW9rfGT2","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have comprehensive information. Let me create a detailed summary of the UI patterns and component structure.\n\n## Comprehensive Summary: Ralph Wiggum Dashboard UI Patterns & Component Structure\n\n### 1. APPLICATION STRUCTURE\n\n**File Location**: `C:\\Users\\xsams\\RalphWiggumV3\\RalphWiggumV2\\dashboard\\src\\`\n\n**Routing Architecture**:\n- **App.tsx** (Main Entry Point): Simple passthrough that renders the Dashboard component\n- **Dashboard.tsx** (Root Component): Contains all tab-based navigation and state management via WebSocket hook\n\nThe application uses a **single-component routing pattern** with conditional rendering based on tab state rather than traditional router.\n\n**Tab Structure** (4 main sections):\n1. **Dashboard Tab** - Loop status, controls, metrics, recent logs\n2. **Generate Tab** - Plan & PRD generation tools\n3. **Logs Tab** - Full log viewer\n4. **Setup Tab** - Configuration wizard and agent management\n\n---\n\n### 2. UI PATTERNS & FRAMEWORKS\n\n#### **Radix UI Components Used**:\n- `@radix-ui/react-tabs` - Tab navigation\n- `@radix-ui/react-checkbox` - Checkboxes\n- `@radix-ui/react-label` - Form labels\n- `@radix-ui/react-select` - Dropdowns\n- `@radix-ui/react-scroll-area` - Scrollable areas\n- `@radix-ui/react-progress` - Progress bars\n- `@radix-ui/react-switch` - Toggle switches\n- `@radix-ui/react-tooltip` - Tooltips\n- `@radix-ui/react-dialog` - Dialogs/modals\n\n#### **Tailwind CSS Integration**:\n- **CSS Variables for theming** (`index.css`):\n  - Color scheme using HSL values\n  - Light theme (default): Light backgrounds, dark text\n  - Dark theme (`.dark` class): Inverted colors\n  - Chart colors, border radius, shadows all configurable\n  \n- **Tailwind Configuration** (`tailwind.config.js`):\n  - Custom color system mapped to CSS variables\n  - Supports dark mode via class strategy\n  - Built-in animation plugin: `tailwindcss-animate`\n  - Rounded corners using CSS variable fallback\n\n#### **Icon Library**:\n- **lucide-react** (v0.562.0) - 24x24 SVG icons with consistent styling\n- Icons integrated into buttons, headers, and status indicators\n\n#### **Class Utility System**:\n- `clsx` - Conditional class merging\n- `tailwind-merge` - Prevent Tailwind class conflicts\n- Custom `cn()` utility (in `lib/utils.ts`) combines both for safe class composition\n\n---\n\n### 3. COMPONENT STRUCTURE\n\n#### **UI Base Components** (`src/components/ui/`):\n\nAll base components follow a **Radix UI + Tailwind pattern**:\n\n1. **Card Components** (`card.tsx`):\n   ```\n   Card → CardHeader → CardTitle/CardDescription\n        → CardContent\n        → CardFooter\n   ```\n   - Used for all content containers\n   - Consistent padding (p-6), rounded borders, shadow\n   - Composable subcomponents\n\n2. **Tabs** (`tabs.tsx`):\n   - Wraps `@radix-ui/react-tabs`\n   - TabsList (container), TabsTrigger (individual tabs), TabsContent (pane)\n   - Keyboard navigation built-in via Radix\n\n3. **Button** (`button.tsx`):\n   - Uses CVA (class-variance-authority) for variants\n   - 6 variants: `default`, `destructive`, `outline`, `secondary`, `ghost`, `link`\n   - 4 sizes: `default`, `sm`, `lg`, `icon`\n   - Accessible focus states with ring indicators\n\n4. **Badge** (`badge.tsx`):\n   - Small status indicators\n   - 6 variants including `success`, `warning`, `destructive`\n   - Used for status tags (e.g., \"Connected\", \"Running\")\n\n5. **Input & Label** (`input.tsx`, `label.tsx`):\n   - Standard form components\n   - Consistent focus states and accessibility\n\n6. **Checkbox & Switch** (`checkbox.tsx`, `switch.tsx`):\n   - Wrapped Radix primitives\n   - Full keyboard support\n\n7. **ScrollArea** (`scroll-area.tsx`):\n   - Custom scrollbar styling\n   - Used in modals, log viewers, text areas\n\n8. **Select** (`select.tsx`):\n   - Radix-based dropdown with full accessibility\n\n9. **Progress** (`progress.tsx`):\n   - Visual progress indicators\n\n10. **Tooltip** (`tooltip.tsx`):\n    - Radix-based tooltips with positioning\n\n#### **Feature Components** (`src/components/`):\n\n**Dashboard Components**:\n- **Dashboard.tsx** - Main container managing all tabs and WebSocket state\n- **LoopControls.tsx** - Control panel for starting/stopping loops\n- **LoopStatus.tsx** - Status card showing loop state, iteration count, duration\n- **LogViewer.tsx** - Scrollable log display with color-coded types (error, warning, success)\n- **ContextMeter.tsx** - Token/context usage visualization\n- **GitHistory.tsx** - Git commit and branch information display\n- **TaskList.tsx** - Tasks from IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n\n**Generation Components**:\n- **PlanGenerator.tsx** - Implementation plan generator UI\n  - Form inputs for goal/scope\n  - Mode selection buttons (Standard, SLC, Work-Scoped)\n  - Output preview with scroll area\n  - Copy/Insert to file buttons\n  \n- **PRDGenerator.tsx** - PRD and Audience JTBD generator\n  - Form for product details\n  - Document selection UI\n  - Dual output (PRD + AUDIENCE)\n  - DocumentPreview modal integration\n\n**Modal/Dialog Components**:\n- **DocumentPreview.tsx** - Full-screen overlay modal\n  - Fixed overlay with backdrop click detection\n  - Scrollable content area\n  - Copy and selection buttons\n  - No Radix Dialog - custom modal implementation\n\n- **ExistingDocsViewer.tsx** - Shows existing documentation\n- **DocumentationSelector.tsx** - Selects docs for PRD context\n\n**Setup Wizard Components**:\n- **OnboardingWizard.tsx** - Multi-step setup wizard\n  - Steps: welcome → scanning → results → configure → docs → complete\n  - Progress bar using Progress component\n  - Form fields with auto-detection\n\n- **SetupWizard.tsx** - Full configuration interface\n- **AgentsConfig.tsx** - Specialist agents toggle\n- **CursorRulesConfig.tsx** - Cursor rules management\n- **DependencyChecker.tsx** - System dependency checking\n- **PromptsConfig.tsx** - Agent prompts configuration\n- **SpecialistAgentsConfig.tsx** - Specialist agent setup\n- **ClaudeMdConfig.tsx** - CLAUDE.md configuration\n\n---\n\n### 4. DIALOG/MODAL PATTERNS\n\n#### **Modal Implementation - DocumentPreview.tsx**:\n```tsx\n// Custom modal (NOT using Radix Dialog)\n<div className=\"fixed inset-0 z-50 bg-black/50 flex items-center justify-center p-4\">\n  <div className=\"bg-background rounded-lg shadow-xl w-full max-w-3xl max-h-[80vh] flex flex-col\">\n    {/* Header with close button */}\n    {/* Scrollable content area */}\n    {/* Footer with actions */}\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n**Key Characteristics**:\n- Full-screen overlay with semi-transparent black backdrop\n- Backdrop click closes modal (`handleBackdropClick`)\n- Max-width constraint for readability\n- Z-index 50 for layering\n- Three-section layout: header, content, footer\n- Content area uses ScrollArea component for overflow\n\n**Action Buttons in Modal**:\n- Copy to clipboard with state feedback (`copied` state → \"Copied!\" message)\n- Toggle selection with visual feedback\n- Close button (X icon)\n\n#### **State Management Pattern**:\n- Modal visibility controlled by parent component (`isOpen` prop)\n- Content loaded asynchronously (`isLoading` prop)\n- Selection state passed via props\n- Callbacks for user actions\n\n---\n\n### 5. STATE MANAGEMENT\n\n**WebSocket Hook** (`useWebSocket.ts`):\n- Central state management for entire dashboard\n- Real-time server communication\n- Returns extensive state object with:\n  - Loop status and controls\n  - Task management\n  - Git information\n  - Log streaming\n  - Plan/PRD generation status\n  - Project configuration\n  - Agent and rules management\n  - Document selection state\n  - File preview state\n\n**Pattern**: Props drilling from Dashboard → child components, with callbacks for mutations\n\n---\n\n### 6. STYLING PATTERNS\n\n#### **Tailwind Utility Patterns**:\n\n```tsx\n// Layout patterns\nclassName=\"grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3\"  // Responsive grid\nclassName=\"flex items-center justify-between\"          // Flex alignment\nclassName=\"space-y-4\"                                  // Vertical spacing\n\n// Card styling\nclassName=\"rounded-lg border bg-card text-card-foreground shadow-sm\"\n\n// Button patterns\nclassName=\"gap-2\"                                      // Icon + text spacing\n\n// Form styling\nclassName=\"flex flex-col space-y-2\"                    // Label + input stacking\n\n// Status/color coding\nclassName=\"text-green-500\"   // Success\nclassName=\"text-red-500\"     // Error\nclassName=\"text-yellow-500\"  // Warning\nclassName=\"text-foreground\"  // Default\n```\n\n#### **Responsive Design**:\n- Mobile-first approach\n- Breakpoints: `sm`, `md`, `lg` (Tailwind defaults)\n- Grid layouts adapt from 1 → 2 → 3 columns\n- Compact and full view options (e.g., LogViewer)\n\n#### **Dark Mode**:\n- Implemented via CSS variable overrides in `.dark` class\n- Applied to root element\n- All colors automatically adjust via Tailwind's theme system\n\n---\n\n### 7. TYPE SYSTEM\n\n**Key Types** (`src/types/index.ts`):\n\n```typescript\n// Loop Management\nLoopMode = 'plan' | 'plan-slc' | 'plan-work' | 'build'\nLoopStatus { running, mode, iteration, maxIterations, workScope, startedAt, pid }\n\n// WebSocket Messages\nServerMessage (discriminated union of all message types)\nClientCommand (discriminated union of all client commands)\n\n// Data Types\nProjectScan, ProjectInfo, ProjectConfig, AgentInfo, CursorRuleInfo\nLogEntry, GitStatus, Task, SpecialistAgent\n\n// Generation\nPlanGeneratorStatus, PRDGeneratorStatus\nDiscoveredDoc, SubProject, RepoAgentInfo\n```\n\nAll types are exported from central index, providing strong typing throughout components.\n\n---\n\n### 8. KEY UI PATTERNS OBSERVED\n\n1. **Card-Based Layout**: Almost all content in Cards with header/content/footer\n2. **Icon + Text**: Consistent pattern for buttons and headings (lucide icons)\n3. **Status Badges**: Color-coded badges for states (success, destructive, secondary)\n4. **Scroll Areas**: Used for long-form content (logs, previews, configs)\n5. **Form Grouping**: `space-y-2` gap between label and input\n6. **Action Groups**: Related buttons grouped with `flex gap-3`\n7. **Progress Indication**: Loading states with `Loader2` spinning icon\n8. **Empty States**: Centered icon + text for empty log/task views\n9. **Two-Column Layouts**: Dashboard uses `lg:grid-cols-2` for content sections\n10. **Tab-Based Navigation**: Main routing mechanism (no URL-based routing)\n\n---\n\n### 9. DEPENDENCIES SUMMARY\n\n**Key Libraries**:\n- **React 19.2**: Latest React with improved features\n- **Vite 7.2**: Build tool and dev server\n- **Tailwind CSS 3.4**: Utility-first CSS framework\n- **Radix UI**: Headless component primitives\n- **Lucide React**: Icon library\n- **WebSocket (ws)**: Real-time server communication\n- **Express 5**: Backend server\n- **TypeScript 5.9**: Static typing\n- **ESLint 9**: Code quality\n\n**Build Commands** (from package.json):\n- `npm run dev` - Concurrent Vite + WebSocket server\n- `npm run build` - TypeScript compilation + Vite build\n- `npm run lint` - ESLint code checking\n\n---\n\n### 10. ACCESSIBILITY PATTERNS\n\n**Implemented via Radix UI**:\n- Keyboard navigation (Tab, Arrow keys)\n- ARIA roles and labels (buttons, tabs, form fields)\n- Focus visible indicators (ring-2 ring-ring)\n- Color contrast (via theme design)\n- Semantic HTML (labels, sections, headings)\n\n---\n\nThis is a **production-quality design system** built on proven technologies (Radix + Tailwind), with strong typing, real-time WebSocket communication, and a clear component hierarchy."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a861cc0 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d9df9ce-f430-4def-aa62-de4fb0297909","uuid":"13267190-3136-4273-9997-43ab535c684d","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the src/components directory to understand:\n1. How Dashboard.tsx is structured\n2. How App.tsx routes between components\n3. What UI patterns are used (Radix, Tailwind)\n4. How existing dialogs/modals are implemented\n\nProvide a comprehensive summary of the UI patterns and component structure.","agentId":"a861cc0","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have comprehensive information. Let me create a detailed summary of the UI patterns and component structure.\n\n## Comprehensive Summary: Ralph Wiggum Dashboard UI Patterns & Component Structure\n\n### 1. APPLICATION STRUCTURE\n\n**File Location**: `C:\\Users\\xsams\\RalphWiggumV3\\RalphWiggumV2\\dashboard\\src\\`\n\n**Routing Architecture**:\n- **App.tsx** (Main Entry Point): Simple passthrough that renders the Dashboard component\n- **Dashboard.tsx** (Root Component): Contains all tab-based navigation and state management via WebSocket hook\n\nThe application uses a **single-component routing pattern** with conditional rendering based on tab state rather than traditional router.\n\n**Tab Structure** (4 main sections):\n1. **Dashboard Tab** - Loop status, controls, metrics, recent logs\n2. **Generate Tab** - Plan & PRD generation tools\n3. **Logs Tab** - Full log viewer\n4. **Setup Tab** - Configuration wizard and agent management\n\n---\n\n### 2. UI PATTERNS & FRAMEWORKS\n\n#### **Radix UI Components Used**:\n- `@radix-ui/react-tabs` - Tab navigation\n- `@radix-ui/react-checkbox` - Checkboxes\n- `@radix-ui/react-label` - Form labels\n- `@radix-ui/react-select` - Dropdowns\n- `@radix-ui/react-scroll-area` - Scrollable areas\n- `@radix-ui/react-progress` - Progress bars\n- `@radix-ui/react-switch` - Toggle switches\n- `@radix-ui/react-tooltip` - Tooltips\n- `@radix-ui/react-dialog` - Dialogs/modals\n\n#### **Tailwind CSS Integration**:\n- **CSS Variables for theming** (`index.css`):\n  - Color scheme using HSL values\n  - Light theme (default): Light backgrounds, dark text\n  - Dark theme (`.dark` class): Inverted colors\n  - Chart colors, border radius, shadows all configurable\n  \n- **Tailwind Configuration** (`tailwind.config.js`):\n  - Custom color system mapped to CSS variables\n  - Supports dark mode via class strategy\n  - Built-in animation plugin: `tailwindcss-animate`\n  - Rounded corners using CSS variable fallback\n\n#### **Icon Library**:\n- **lucide-react** (v0.562.0) - 24x24 SVG icons with consistent styling\n- Icons integrated into buttons, headers, and status indicators\n\n#### **Class Utility System**:\n- `clsx` - Conditional class merging\n- `tailwind-merge` - Prevent Tailwind class conflicts\n- Custom `cn()` utility (in `lib/utils.ts`) combines both for safe class composition\n\n---\n\n### 3. COMPONENT STRUCTURE\n\n#### **UI Base Components** (`src/components/ui/`):\n\nAll base components follow a **Radix UI + Tailwind pattern**:\n\n1. **Card Components** (`card.tsx`):\n   ```\n   Card → CardHeader → CardTitle/CardDescription\n        → CardContent\n        → CardFooter\n   ```\n   - Used for all content containers\n   - Consistent padding (p-6), rounded borders, shadow\n   - Composable subcomponents\n\n2. **Tabs** (`tabs.tsx`):\n   - Wraps `@radix-ui/react-tabs`\n   - TabsList (container), TabsTrigger (individual tabs), TabsContent (pane)\n   - Keyboard navigation built-in via Radix\n\n3. **Button** (`button.tsx`):\n   - Uses CVA (class-variance-authority) for variants\n   - 6 variants: `default`, `destructive`, `outline`, `secondary`, `ghost`, `link`\n   - 4 sizes: `default`, `sm`, `lg`, `icon`\n   - Accessible focus states with ring indicators\n\n4. **Badge** (`badge.tsx`):\n   - Small status indicators\n   - 6 variants including `success`, `warning`, `destructive`\n   - Used for status tags (e.g., \"Connected\", \"Running\")\n\n5. **Input & Label** (`input.tsx`, `label.tsx`):\n   - Standard form components\n   - Consistent focus states and accessibility\n\n6. **Checkbox & Switch** (`checkbox.tsx`, `switch.tsx`):\n   - Wrapped Radix primitives\n   - Full keyboard support\n\n7. **ScrollArea** (`scroll-area.tsx`):\n   - Custom scrollbar styling\n   - Used in modals, log viewers, text areas\n\n8. **Select** (`select.tsx`):\n   - Radix-based dropdown with full accessibility\n\n9. **Progress** (`progress.tsx`):\n   - Visual progress indicators\n\n10. **Tooltip** (`tooltip.tsx`):\n    - Radix-based tooltips with positioning\n\n#### **Feature Components** (`src/components/`):\n\n**Dashboard Components**:\n- **Dashboard.tsx** - Main container managing all tabs and WebSocket state\n- **LoopControls.tsx** - Control panel for starting/stopping loops\n- **LoopStatus.tsx** - Status card showing loop state, iteration count, duration\n- **LogViewer.tsx** - Scrollable log display with color-coded types (error, warning, success)\n- **ContextMeter.tsx** - Token/context usage visualization\n- **GitHistory.tsx** - Git commit and branch information display\n- **TaskList.tsx** - Tasks from IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n\n**Generation Components**:\n- **PlanGenerator.tsx** - Implementation plan generator UI\n  - Form inputs for goal/scope\n  - Mode selection buttons (Standard, SLC, Work-Scoped)\n  - Output preview with scroll area\n  - Copy/Insert to file buttons\n  \n- **PRDGenerator.tsx** - PRD and Audience JTBD generator\n  - Form for product details\n  - Document selection UI\n  - Dual output (PRD + AUDIENCE)\n  - DocumentPreview modal integration\n\n**Modal/Dialog Components**:\n- **DocumentPreview.tsx** - Full-screen overlay modal\n  - Fixed overlay with backdrop click detection\n  - Scrollable content area\n  - Copy and selection buttons\n  - No Radix Dialog - custom modal implementation\n\n- **ExistingDocsViewer.tsx** - Shows existing documentation\n- **DocumentationSelector.tsx** - Selects docs for PRD context\n\n**Setup Wizard Components**:\n- **OnboardingWizard.tsx** - Multi-step setup wizard\n  - Steps: welcome → scanning → results → configure → docs → complete\n  - Progress bar using Progress component\n  - Form fields with auto-detection\n\n- **SetupWizard.tsx** - Full configuration interface\n- **AgentsConfig.tsx** - Specialist agents toggle\n- **CursorRulesConfig.tsx** - Cursor rules management\n- **DependencyChecker.tsx** - System dependency checking\n- **PromptsConfig.tsx** - Agent prompts configuration\n- **SpecialistAgentsConfig.tsx** - Specialist agent setup\n- **ClaudeMdConfig.tsx** - CLAUDE.md configuration\n\n---\n\n### 4. DIALOG/MODAL PATTERNS\n\n#### **Modal Implementation - DocumentPreview.tsx**:\n```tsx\n// Custom modal (NOT using Radix Dialog)\n<div className=\"fixed inset-0 z-50 bg-black/50 flex items-center justify-center p-4\">\n  <div className=\"bg-background rounded-lg shadow-xl w-full max-w-3xl max-h-[80vh] flex flex-col\">\n    {/* Header with close button */}\n    {/* Scrollable content area */}\n    {/* Footer with actions */}\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n**Key Characteristics**:\n- Full-screen overlay with semi-transparent black backdrop\n- Backdrop click closes modal (`handleBackdropClick`)\n- Max-width constraint for readability\n- Z-index 50 for layering\n- Three-section layout: header, content, footer\n- Content area uses ScrollArea component for overflow\n\n**Action Buttons in Modal**:\n- Copy to clipboard with state feedback (`copied` state → \"Copied!\" message)\n- Toggle selection with visual feedback\n- Close button (X icon)\n\n#### **State Management Pattern**:\n- Modal visibility controlled by parent component (`isOpen` prop)\n- Content loaded asynchronously (`isLoading` prop)\n- Selection state passed via props\n- Callbacks for user actions\n\n---\n\n### 5. STATE MANAGEMENT\n\n**WebSocket Hook** (`useWebSocket.ts`):\n- Central state management for entire dashboard\n- Real-time server communication\n- Returns extensive state object with:\n  - Loop status and controls\n  - Task management\n  - Git information\n  - Log streaming\n  - Plan/PRD generation status\n  - Project configuration\n  - Agent and rules management\n  - Document selection state\n  - File preview state\n\n**Pattern**: Props drilling from Dashboard → child components, with callbacks for mutations\n\n---\n\n### 6. STYLING PATTERNS\n\n#### **Tailwind Utility Patterns**:\n\n```tsx\n// Layout patterns\nclassName=\"grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3\"  // Responsive grid\nclassName=\"flex items-center justify-between\"          // Flex alignment\nclassName=\"space-y-4\"                                  // Vertical spacing\n\n// Card styling\nclassName=\"rounded-lg border bg-card text-card-foreground shadow-sm\"\n\n// Button patterns\nclassName=\"gap-2\"                                      // Icon + text spacing\n\n// Form styling\nclassName=\"flex flex-col space-y-2\"                    // Label + input stacking\n\n// Status/color coding\nclassName=\"text-green-500\"   // Success\nclassName=\"text-red-500\"     // Error\nclassName=\"text-yellow-500\"  // Warning\nclassName=\"text-foreground\"  // Default\n```\n\n#### **Responsive Design**:\n- Mobile-first approach\n- Breakpoints: `sm`, `md`, `lg` (Tailwind defaults)\n- Grid layouts adapt from 1 → 2 → 3 columns\n- Compact and full view options (e.g., LogViewer)\n\n#### **Dark Mode**:\n- Implemented via CSS variable overrides in `.dark` class\n- Applied to root element\n- All colors automatically adjust via Tailwind's theme system\n\n---\n\n### 7. TYPE SYSTEM\n\n**Key Types** (`src/types/index.ts`):\n\n```typescript\n// Loop Management\nLoopMode = 'plan' | 'plan-slc' | 'plan-work' | 'build'\nLoopStatus { running, mode, iteration, maxIterations, workScope, startedAt, pid }\n\n// WebSocket Messages\nServerMessage (discriminated union of all message types)\nClientCommand (discriminated union of all client commands)\n\n// Data Types\nProjectScan, ProjectInfo, ProjectConfig, AgentInfo, CursorRuleInfo\nLogEntry, GitStatus, Task, SpecialistAgent\n\n// Generation\nPlanGeneratorStatus, PRDGeneratorStatus\nDiscoveredDoc, SubProject, RepoAgentInfo\n```\n\nAll types are exported from central index, providing strong typing throughout components.\n\n---\n\n### 8. KEY UI PATTERNS OBSERVED\n\n1. **Card-Based Layout**: Almost all content in Cards with header/content/footer\n2. **Icon + Text**: Consistent pattern for buttons and headings (lucide icons)\n3. **Status Badges**: Color-coded badges for states (success, destructive, secondary)\n4. **Scroll Areas**: Used for long-form content (logs, previews, configs)\n5. **Form Grouping**: `space-y-2` gap between label and input\n6. **Action Groups**: Related buttons grouped with `flex gap-3`\n7. **Progress Indication**: Loading states with `Loader2` spinning icon\n8. **Empty States**: Centered icon + text for empty log/task views\n9. **Two-Column Layouts**: Dashboard uses `lg:grid-cols-2` for content sections\n10. **Tab-Based Navigation**: Main routing mechanism (no URL-based routing)\n\n---\n\n### 9. DEPENDENCIES SUMMARY\n\n**Key Libraries**:\n- **React 19.2**: Latest React with improved features\n- **Vite 7.2**: Build tool and dev server\n- **Tailwind CSS 3.4**: Utility-first CSS framework\n- **Radix UI**: Headless component primitives\n- **Lucide React**: Icon library\n- **WebSocket (ws)**: Real-time server communication\n- **Express 5**: Backend server\n- **TypeScript 5.9**: Static typing\n- **ESLint 9**: Code quality\n\n**Build Commands** (from package.json):\n- `npm run dev` - Concurrent Vite + WebSocket server\n- `npm run build` - TypeScript compilation + Vite build\n- `npm run lint` - ESLint code checking\n\n---\n\n### 10. ACCESSIBILITY PATTERNS\n\n**Implemented via Radix UI**:\n- Keyboard navigation (Tab, Arrow keys)\n- ARIA roles and labels (buttons, tabs, form fields)\n- Focus visible indicators (ring-2 ring-ring)\n- Color contrast (via theme design)\n- Semantic HTML (labels, sections, headings)\n\n---\n\nThis is a **production-quality design system** built on proven technologies (Radix + Tailwind), with strong typing, real-time WebSocket communication, and a clear component hierarchy."}],"totalDurationMs":101883,"totalTokens":61522,"totalToolUseCount":27,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1974,"cache_read_input_tokens":56350,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1974,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3191,"service_tier":"standard"}}}
