type: 'agents:toggle', payload: { agentId, enabled } })\n```\n\n**Helper Functions:**\nThe hook also provides specialized helper functions that internally use `sendCommand`:\n- `scanProject()`, `listAgents()`, `listRules()`\n- `readDoc(docPath)`, `closeDocPreview()`\n- `listClaudeMdFiles()`, `readClaudeMdFile(filePath)`, `applyRalphClaudeMd()`\n- `checkDependencies()`, `readConfigFile(filename)`\n- `installAgentGlobal(agentId)`, `installAgentProject(agentId)`, `installAllAgentsGlobal()`\n\n### 2. Overall Component Structure and Layout\n\n**Hierarchical Structure:**\n\n```\nDashboard (root container)\n├── Header (fixed top banner)\n│   ├── Logo & Title\n│   ├── GitHub repo link (if available)\n│   ├── Connection status badge\n│   └── Loop status badge\n│\n└── Main Content (container with tabs)\n    ├── TabsList (4 main navigation tabs)\n    └── Tab Content Areas:\n        ├── Dashboard Tab\n        │   ├── LoopControls\n        │   ├── ExistingDocsViewer\n        │   ├── Status Grid (3 columns)\n        │   │   ├── LoopStatus\n        │   │   ├── ContextMeter\n        │   │   └── GitHistory\n        │   └── Two-column layout\n        │       ├── TaskList\n        │       └── Recent Logs (LogViewer)\n        │\n        ├── Generate Tab (nested tabs)\n        │   ├── Implementation Plan sub-tab\n        │   │   └── PlanGenerator\n        │   └── PRD & Audience sub-tab\n        │       └── PRDGenerator\n        │\n        ├── Logs Tab\n        │   └── LogViewer (full logs)\n        │\n        └── Setup Tab\n            └── SetupWizard\n```\n\n**Conditional Rendering:**\n- Shows `OnboardingWizard` if `showOnboarding` is true (when AGENTS.md doesn't exist)\n- Otherwise shows the main dashboard layout\n\n**Layout Classes:**\n- Root: `min-h-screen bg-background`\n- Header: `border-b bg-card px-6 py-4`\n- Main content: `container mx-auto p-6`\n- Status grid: `grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3`\n- Tasks section: `grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2`\n\n### 3. How Tabs/Navigation Work\n\n**Two-Level Tab System:**\n\n**Primary Tabs (shadcn/ui Tabs component):**\n- Controlled via `activeTab` state (lines 89, 188)\n- Four main tabs: `dashboard`, `generate`, `logs`, `setup`\n- Uses shadcn's `<Tabs>`, `<TabsList>`, `<TabsTrigger>`, `<TabsContent>` components\n\n```typescript\n<Tabs value={activeTab} onValueChange={setActiveTab}>\n  <TabsList className=\"grid w-full grid-cols-4 lg:w-[500px]\">\n    <TabsTrigger value=\"dashboard\" className=\"gap-2\">\n      <LayoutDashboard className=\"h-4 w-4\" />\n      Dashboard\n    </TabsTrigger>\n    {/* ... more tabs */}\n  </TabsList>\n  <TabsContent value=\"dashboard\">...</TabsContent>\n</Tabs>\n```\n\n**Secondary Tabs (inside Generate tab):**\n- Nested tabs within the \"Generate\" tab\n- Two sub-tabs: `plan` (Implementation Plan) and `prd` (PRD & Audience)\n- Uses `defaultValue=\"plan\"` (uncontrolled, no explicit state management)\n- Structured identically to primary tabs but with different content\n\n**Tab Features:**\n- Icons from `lucide-react` for visual identification\n- Programmatic navigation: `setActiveTab('generate')` (line 222)\n- Auto-triggering: Project scan triggers when entering generate tab (lines 103-107)\n- Responsive width: Full width on mobile, fixed `lg:w-[500px]` on desktop\n\n**Tab State Management:**\n```typescript\nconst [activeTab, setActiveTab] = useState('dashboard');\n\n// Programmatic navigation example\nonNavigateToGenerate={(tab) => {\n  setActiveTab('generate');\n  // Inner tabs default based on tab parameter\n}}\n```\n\n### 4. UI Patterns Used\n\n**Tailwind CSS Patterns:**\n\n**Layout Utilities:**\n- Flexbox: `flex items-center justify-between`, `flex items-center gap-3`\n- Grid: `grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3`, `grid w-full grid-cols-4`\n- Spacing: `px-6 py-4`, `p-6`, `space-y-6`, `gap-1`, `gap-2`, `gap-3`, `gap-4`\n- Container: `container mx-auto`\n- Responsive: `md:grid-cols-2`, `lg:grid-cols-3`, `lg:w-[500px]`\n\n**Typography:**\n- Headers: `text-xl font-semibold`, `text-lg font-semibold`\n- Muted text: `text-sm text-muted-foreground`\n- Icons: `h-4 w-4`, `h-5 w-5`, `h-10 w-10`\n\n**Colors & Theming:**\n- Background: `bg-background`, `bg-card`, `bg-primary`\n- Text: `text-primary-foreground`, `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`\n- Borders: `border-b`\n- Hover states: `hover:text-foreground transition-colors`\n\n**Component Sizing:**\n- Fixed icon containers: `flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg`\n- Responsive widths: `w-full`, `lg:w-[500px]`\n\n**shadcn/ui Components Used:**\n\n1. **Tabs** (lines 14, 188, 258): Primary navigation system\n2. **Badge** (lines 15, 166, 179): Status indicators with variants:\n   - `variant=\"success\"` for connected\n   - `variant=\"destructive\"` for disconnected\n   - `variant=\"default\"` for running loop\n   - `variant=\"secondary\"` for idle\n\n**Custom Components:**\n- `LoopStatus`, `TaskList`, `LogViewer`, `ContextMeter`, `GitHistory`\n- `LoopControls`, `SetupWizard`, `OnboardingWizard`\n- `PlanGenerator`, `PRDGenerator`, `ExistingDocsViewer`\n\n**Icons from lucide-react:**\n- Navigation: `LayoutDashboard`, `Settings`, `Terminal`, `Wand2`\n- Status: `Wifi`, `WifiOff`, `Github`\n- Content types: `ListTodo`, `FileText`\n\n**Key Design Patterns:**\n\n1. **Conditional Badge Variants:**\n```typescript\n<Badge variant={connected ? 'success' : 'destructive'}>\n  {connected ? <><Wifi /></> : <><WifiOff /></>}\n</Badge>\n```\n\n2. **Icon-Text Pairing:**\n```typescript\n<TabsTrigger value=\"dashboard\" className=\"gap-2\">\n  <LayoutDashboard className=\"h-4 w-4\" />\n  Dashboard\n</TabsTrigger>\n```\n\n3. **External Links:**\n```typescript\n<a href=\"...\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" \n   className=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm...\">\n```\n\n4. **Responsive Grid Layouts:**\n```typescript\n// 1 col mobile, 2 col tablet, 3 col desktop\nclassName=\"grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3\"\n```\n\n5. **State-Driven Rendering:**\n- Uses loading states: `scanLoading`, `agentsLoading`, etc.\n- Conditional content: `showOnboarding` determines entire view\n- Data-driven lists: `logs.slice(-20)` for recent logs\n\n### Key Patterns for Creating Similar Launcher Components\n\n**1. WebSocket Integration Pattern:**\n- Extract all WebSocket logic into a custom hook\n- Return both state and command functions\n- Use TypeScript for strongly-typed messages\n- Include reconnection logic and cleanup\n\n**2. Tab-Based Navigation:**\n- Use shadcn/ui Tabs for consistent UX\n- Pair icons with text labels\n- Support nested tabs where appropriate\n- Use controlled tabs for programmatic navigation\n\n**3. Status Indicators:**\n- Use Badges with semantic variants (success, destructive, default, secondary)\n- Pair status with icons (Wifi/WifiOff pattern)\n- Display multiple statuses in header\n\n**4. Responsive Layout:**\n- Mobile-first with `md:` and `lg:` breakpoints\n- Grid layouts that adapt: 1 col → 2 col → 3 col\n- Fixed widths on desktop, full width on mobile\n\n**5. Component Organization:**\n- Split complex UI into focused sub-components\n- Pass WebSocket state/handlers as props\n- Keep Dashboard as orchestrator, not implementer\n\n**6. Loading & Error States:**\n- Track loading state per operation (scanLoading, agentsLoading, etc.)\n- Show errors via dedicated state variables\n- Provide clear feedback on async operations\n\n**7. Tailwind Consistency:**\n- Use theme variables: `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `border`\n- Consistent spacing scale: `gap-2`, `gap-4`, `gap-6`\n- Standard icon sizes: `h-4 w-4` for inline, `h-5 w-5` for headers\n\nThis Dashboard component serves as an excellent reference architecture for building real-time monitoring dashboards with WebSocket communication, multi-level navigation, and responsive layouts."}],"totalDurationMs":68866,"totalTokens":28545,"totalToolUseCount":3,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7976,"cache_read_input_tokens":17670,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7976,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2895,"service_tier":"standard"}}}
