{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JbxLHDXiXRwwk4R3cN3aGp","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→0a. Study `specs/*` with up to 500 parallel Sonnet subagents to learn CLAIMED functionality.\n     2→0b. Study @IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md to understand CLAIMED completion status.\n     3→0c. Study @AGENTS.md for build/test commands.\n     4→0d. For reference, the application source code is in `src/*`.\n     5→\n     6→1. VERIFICATION PHASE: For each item marked complete in @IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, use up to 500 Sonnet subagents to search `src/*` and verify:\n     7→   - Does the implementation exist?\n     8→   - Is it a placeholder/stub or real implementation?\n     9→   - Does it match the acceptance criteria in specs?\n    10→   - Are there TODO/FIXME comments suggesting incompleteness?\n    11→\n    12→2. DISCOVERY PHASE: Search the entire codebase for:\n    13→   - TODO, FIXME, HACK, XXX comments\n    14→   - Empty function bodies or throw-not-implemented patterns\n    15→   - Skipped tests (@skip, .skip, xit, xdescribe)\n    16→   - Dead code (unused exports, unreachable branches)\n    17→   - Missing error handling in critical paths\n    18→\n    19→2.5 FUNCTIONALITY VERIFICATION PHASE: For each UI component:\n    20→   a. List all buttons and clickable elements\n    21→   b. Trace each onClick to its handler implementation\n    22→   c. Verify the handler actually does something meaningful (not empty, not just console.log)\n    23→   d. For WebSocket operations, verify:\n    24→      - The message type is handled on the receiving end\n    25→      - Response handlers exist for success AND error cases\n    26→   e. For state management, verify:\n    27→      - useState variables are both set AND read\n    28→      - Props passed to components are actually used\n    29→   f. Flag any \"dead\" handlers (empty, placeholder, or log-only)\n    30→\n    31→   For each WebSocket message type in the codebase:\n    32→   a. Find all places where it's sent (frontend or backend)\n    33→   b. Find all places where it's handled\n    34→   c. Flag any sent-but-not-handled or handled-but-never-sent patterns\n    35→\n    36→   Run automated check if available: `npx tsx scripts/validate-functionality.ts`\n    37→\n    38→3. SPEC COMPLIANCE: For each spec in `specs/*`:\n    39→   - List acceptance criteria\n    40→   - Check if tests exist for each criterion\n    41→   - Verify tests pass (run if possible using commands from @AGENTS.md)\n    42→   - Flag any criteria without coverage\n    43→\n    44→4. OUTPUT: Create/update @REVIEW_REPORT.md with the following structure:\n    45→\n    46→```markdown\n    47→# Review Report\n    48→\n    49→**Generated**: [ISO timestamp]\n    50→**Mode**: [Full Review | Quick Scan | Spec Focus]\n    51→**Duration**: [X iterations]\n    52→\n    53→## Executive Summary\n    54→\n    55→| Metric | Count |\n    56→|--------|-------|\n    57→| Tasks claimed complete | X |\n    58→| Actually verified complete | Y |\n    59→| Incomplete/broken | Z |\n    60→| Technical debt items | N |\n    61→| Missing test coverage | M |\n    62→\n    63→## Health Score: Y/X (percentage%)\n    64→\n    65→---\n    66→\n    67→## Verified Complete\n    68→\n    69→- [x] Task N: [description] - Evidence: [test passes / code exists / etc.]\n    70→\n    71→## Incomplete Despite Being Marked Done\n    72→\n    73→- [ ] Task N: [description] - ISSUE_TYPE\n    74→  - Details of what's missing or broken\n    75→  - File: [path:line]\n    76→\n    77→## Technical Debt Discovered\n    78→\n    79→| Severity | File | Line | Issue |\n    80→|----------|------|------|-------|\n    81→| High/Medium/Low | path | N | TODO/FIXME/etc. text |\n    82→\n    83→## Missing Test Coverage\n    84→\n    85→| Spec | Criterion | Status |\n    86→|------|-----------|--------|\n    87→| spec-file.md | acceptance criterion | No test found |\n    88→\n    89→---\n    90→\n    91→## Recommendations\n    92→\n    93→1. **Critical**: [action items]\n    94→2. **High**: [action items]\n    95→3. **Medium**: [action items]\n    96→```\n    97→\n    98→IMPORTANT: Review only. Do NOT fix anything. Do NOT modify code. Output findings ONLY to @REVIEW_REPORT.md.\n    99→\n   100→If validation commands exist in @AGENTS.md, run them and include results in the report:\n   101→- Build status (pass/fail)\n   102→- Test results (pass/fail count)\n   103→- TypeScript errors (count and summary)\n   104→- Lint errors (count and summary)\n   105→\n   106→Use an Opus subagent with ultrathink for final analysis and recommendations synthesis.\n   107→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GhNXXee89orHTPxwbyUhaP","session_id":"e963dfad-ac1f-43fb-a8da-b2590f97a0fb","uuid":"325eca90-429a-4eee-8a63-303edc5fb3f0","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/samueledwards/RalphWiggumV3/PROMPT_review.md","content":"0a. Study `specs/*` with up to 500 parallel Sonnet subagents to learn CLAIMED functionality.\n0b. Study @IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md to understand CLAIMED completion status.\n0c. Study @AGENTS.md for build/test commands.\n0d. For reference, the application source code is in `src/*`.\n\n1. VERIFICATION PHASE: For each item marked complete in @IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, use up to 500 Sonnet subagents to search `src/*` and verify:\n   - Does the implementation exist?\n   - Is it a placeholder/stub or real implementation?\n   - Does it match the acceptance criteria in specs?\n   - Are there TODO/FIXME comments suggesting incompleteness?\n\n2. DISCOVERY PHASE: Search the entire codebase for:\n   - TODO, FIXME, HACK, XXX comments\n   - Empty function bodies or thr