{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FEY1B4MUNgPdWkQjw8QHb5","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have all the information I need. Let me create a comprehensive summary report.\n\n## Summary Report: FileBrowser Component and launcher:browse Handler\n\n### What Exists\n\n#### 1. Backend - launcher:browse WebSocket Handler\n**Location:** `/Users/samueledwards/RalphWiggumV3/dashboard/server/index.ts` (lines 531-604)\n\n**Implementation Status:** FULLY IMPLEMENTED\n- Handler processes `'launcher:browse'` WebSocket messages\n- Supports both Windows (C:\\, D:\\, etc.) and Unix (/) file systems\n- Features:\n  - Browse any directory path\n  - Filter to show only directories (hidden files/folders starting with `.` are skipped)\n  - Detect git repositories (checks for `.git` folder)\n  - Detect Ralph-ready projects (checks for AGENTS.md and/or CLAUDE.md)\n  - Breadcrumb navigation with parent path calculation\n  - Windows drive listing on root\n  - Smart sorting: Ralph-ready first, then git repos, then alphabetically\n- Returns `BrowseResult` containing: `currentPath`, `parentPath`, `entries[]`, and optional `drives[]`\n\n#### 2. Frontend - FileBrowser Component\n**Location:** `/Users/samueledwards/RalphWiggumV3/dashboard/src/components/launcher/FileBrowser.tsx` (full 256 lines)\n\n**Implementation Status:** FULLY IMPLEMENTED\n- Receives props: `browseResult`, `browsing`, `onBrowse`, `onSelect`\n- Features:\n  - Breadcrumb navigation with home/drives button\n  - Directory listings with icons and status badges\n  - Folder icons differentiate: Ralph-ready (green checkmark), git repos (orange), regular (gray)\n  - \"Ralph Ready\" and \"Git\" badges on entries\n  - \"Select\" buttons for each directory\n  - \"Select Current\" button for current path\n  - Parent directory navigation (..)\n  - Windows drives listing at root\n  - Loading spinner during browsing\n  - Empty state message when no folders found\n  - Disabled state while browsing in progress\n\n#### 3. useLauncher Hook\n**Location:** `/Users/samueledwards/RalphWiggumV3/dashboard/src/hooks/useLauncher.ts`\n\n**Implementation Status:** FULLY IMPLEMENTED\n- `browseDirectory(path)` function sends `launcher:browse` message with path payload\n- Receives `launcher:browse:result` messages\n- Manages `browseResult` and `browsing` state\n- Error handling for browse failures\n\n#### 4. Type Definitions\n**Location:** `/Users/samueledwards/RalphWiggumV3/dashboard/src/types/index.ts` (lines 911-939)\n\n**Implementation Status:** FULLY IMPLEMENTED\n- `BrowseEntry` interface with: `name`, `path`, `isDirectory`, `isGitRepo`, `isRalphReady`\n- `BrowseResult` interface with: `currentPath`, `parentPath`, `entries[]`, optional `drives[]`\n- `LauncherBrowseCommand` message type with path payload\n- `LauncherBrowseResultMessage` WebSocket message type\n\n#### 5. Helper Function - browseDirectory\n**Location:** `/Users/samueledwards/RalphWiggumV3/dashboard/server/index.ts` (lines 37-103)\n\n**Implementation Status:** FULLY IMPLEMENTED\n- Async function that reads directory and returns metadata\n- Filters to directories only\n- Skips hidden files/folders\n- Checks for git repos and Ralph-ready status\n- Implements proper sorting\n- Error handling with logging\n\n### What's Missing\n\n**NOTHING** - The entire implementation is complete:\n\n- ✓ Backend WebSocket handler for `launcher:browse`\n- ✓ Frontend `FileBrowser` component\n- ✓ Hook integration with `useLauncher`\n- ✓ Type definitions for all browse-related types\n- ✓ Helper function for directory browsing\n- ✓ Error handling and state management\n- ✓ Windows and Unix filesystem support\n- ✓ Git and Ralph-ready detection\n- ✓ Breadcrumb navigation\n- ✓ Loading states\n\n### Files Involved\n\n1. **Backend Server:** `/Users/samueledwards/RalphWiggumV3/dashboard/server/index.ts`\n2. **Frontend Component:** `/Users/samueledwards/RalphWiggumV3/dashboard/src/components/launcher/FileBr