{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JW45m7oqV8Lp5cjBGTvkvc","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have enough information. Let me create a comprehensive summary report.\n\n## Summary: LLM-as-Judge Review System Analysis\n\nBased on my thorough search of the codebase, here's what exists and what's missing:\n\n### WHAT EXISTS - Comprehensive LLM-as-Judge Infrastructure\n\n**1. Backend Review Runner (ReviewRunner) - COMPLETE**\n- File: `/Users/samueledwards/RalphWiggumV3/dashboard/server/reviewRunner.ts`\n- Features:\n  - Full EventEmitter-based async architecture for quality reviews\n  - Supports both text and image artifact evaluation\n  - Uses Claude CLI with stream-json output parsing\n  - Binary pass/fail results with optional feedback\n  - Handles platform-specific process management (Windows taskill, Unix signals)\n  - Proper JSON parsing with fallback patterns\n  - Status tracking and cancellation support\n\n**2. Frontend Review Panel Component - COMPLETE**\n- File: `/Users/samueledwards/RalphWiggumV3/dashboard/src/components/ReviewPanel.tsx`\n- Features:\n  - Full React component with criteria and artifact input\n  - Artifact type toggle (text vs image path)\n  - 6 preset criteria (UX Clarity, Error Messaging, Visual Hierarchy, Accessibility, Tone, Completeness)\n  - Real-time output display and streaming feedback\n  - Pass/fail result visualization with color coding\n  - Cancel functionality during review runs\n  - Proper loading states and error handling\n\n**3. Type Definitions - COMPLETE**\n- File: `/Users/samueledwards/RalphWiggumV3/dashboard/src/types/index.ts` (lines 945-995)\n- Types included:\n  - `ReviewConfig` - Configuration interface\n  - `ReviewResult` - Result interface with pass/fail + feedback\n  - `ReviewRunnerStatus` - Status tracking\n  - WebSocket message types: `ReviewStatusMessage`, `ReviewOutputMessage`, `ReviewCompleteMessage`, `ReviewErrorMessage`\n  - WebSocket command types: `ReviewRunCommand`, `ReviewCancelCommand`\n\n**4. WebSocket Integration - COMPLETE**\n- File: `/Users/samueledwards/RalphWiggumV3/dashboard/server/index.ts` (lines 652-904)\n- Handlers implemented:\n  - `case 'review:run'` - Runs review with ReviewRunner\n  - `case 'review:cancel'` - Cancels active review\n  - Event broadcasting for status, output, complete, error, and cancelled states\n  - Full integration with broadcast system to all connected clients\n\n**5. Utility Library (LLM Review Stub) - PLACEHOLDER**\n- File: `/Users/samueledwards/RalphWiggumV3/src/lib/llm-review.ts`\n- Status: **NOT IMPLEMENTED - Contains placeholder stub**\n- Notes:\n  - Exports `createReview()` function signature\n  - Mentions support for \"fast\" (Gemini 3.0 Flash) vs \"smart\" (GPT 5.1) modes\n  - References Anthropic API but not implemented\n  - Throws `Error(\"LLM review not implemented...\")`\n  - Test file exists (`llm-review.test.ts`) showing usage patterns\n\n**6. Code Review Generator - COMPLETE (Separate Feature)**\n- File: `/Users/samueledwards/RalphWiggumV3/dashboard/server/reviewGenerator.ts`\n- This is a DIFFERENT system for code reviews (Feature Set 14), not the LLM-as-Judge\n- Generates comprehensive review reports analyzing IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md vs actual implementation\n- Supports modes: `review`, `review-quick`, `review-spec`\n\n---\n\n### WHAT'S MISSING\n\n**1. ReviewPanel is NOT integrated into Dashboard UI**\n- File: `/Users/samueledwards/RalphWiggumV3/dashboard/src/components/ReviewPanel.tsx` exists\n- **BUT** - It's not imported or used in `/Users/samueledwards/RalphWiggumV3/dashboard/src/components/Dashboard.tsx`\n- Dashboard has 4 tabs: Dashboard, Generate, Logs, Setup\n- Generate tab has 3 sub-tabs: Implementation Plan, Code Review, PRD & Audience\n- ReviewPanel is orphaned - no tab in the UI\n\n**2. WebSocket Message Handling in Frontend - MISSING**\n- The frontend `useWebSocket` hook needs to handle:\n  - `review:status` messages\n  - `review:output` messages\n  - `review:complete` messages\n  - `review:error` messages\n- These state management pieces are likely missing from the hook\n\n**3. Native LLM Integration - MISSING**\n- `/Users/samueledwards/RalphWiggumV3/src/lib/llm-review.ts` is a stub\n- Needs actual implementation calling:\n  - Claude API (Anthropic) for intelligent reviews\n  - Support for vision/image evaluation\n  - Support for model selection (fast vs smart modes)\n- Current implementation only uses Claude CLI (external process)\n\n**4. Integration with Dashboard Workflow**\n- No connection between ReviewPanel and existing workflow\n- Could be added as a new tab or integrated into dashboard\n\n---\n\n### ARCHITECTURE SUMMARY\n\nThe system has a **two-tier review architecture**:\n\n1. **LLM-as-Judge Review (Feature Set 13)** - What you asked about\n   - Evaluates subjective criteria (tone, UX, aesthetics, accessibility)\n   - Uses binary pass/fail with feedback\n   - Already has: Backend (ReviewRunner) + Frontend UI (ReviewPanel) + WebSocket handlers\n   - Missing: UI integration + frontend state management\n\n2. **Code Review Generator (Feature Set 14)** - Different system\n   - Analyzes implementation completeness vs claimed tasks\n   - Generates comprehensive reports\n   - Used for project health checks\n\n---\n\n### QUICK CHECKLIST\n\n| Component | Status | Location |\n|-----------|--------|----------|\n| ReviewRunner backend | ✅ Complete | `dashboard/server/reviewRunner.ts` |\n| ReviewPanel component | ✅ Complete | `dashboard/src/components/ReviewPanel.tsx` |\n| Type definitions | ✅ Complete | `dashboard/src/types/index.ts` |\n| WebSocket server handlers | ✅ Complete | `dashboard/server/index.ts` (lines 652-662) |\n| Dashboard UI tab | ❌ Missing | N/A |\n| Frontend state management | ❌ Missing | `useWebSocket` hook |\n| Native LLM integration | ❌ Missing | `src/lib/llm-review.ts` (stub only) |\n| Test coverage | ⚠️ Partial | `src/lib/llm-review.test.ts` (examples only) |\n\nThe infras