{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nAnalysis:\nLet me chronologically analyze the conversation:\n\n1. **Initial Context**: The user provided access to IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, AGENTS.md, and CLAUDE.md files showing RalphWiggumV3 project at 100% completion (94/94 tasks).\n\n2. **User's Initial Request**: The user asked me to implement functionality per specifications, following IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, run tests, validate, and commit changes. The instructions emphasized checking for incomplete tasks and running validation.\n\n3. **My Initial Analysis**:\n   - I searched for specs, cursor rules, and tasks.json\n   - Found tasks.json showed 67/85 tasks done with 18 pending (tasks 83-96)\n   - IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md showed 100% complete, so there was a mismatch\n\n4. **Investigation Phase**:\n   - I used parallel subagent searches to check Feature Set 12 (File Browser), Feature Set 13 (LLM-as-Judge), and Feature Set 14 (Code Review Mode)\n   - Found that most features were already implemented:\n     - Feature Set 12: Fully implemented\n     - Feature Set 13: Backend (ReviewRunner) and component (ReviewPanel) exist, but ReviewPanel NOT integrated into Dashboard\n     - Feature Set 14: Fully implemented\n\n5. **The Gap Identified**: ReviewPanel component existed but was NOT wired into the Dashboard UI. The useWebSocket hook was missing `review:*` message handlers.\n\n6. **Implementation Work**:\n   - Added imports to useWebSocket.ts for ReviewRunnerStatus, ReviewConfig, ReviewResult\n   - Added interface properties for reviewRunnerStatus, reviewRunnerOutput, reviewRunnerResult, reviewRunnerError, runReview, cancelReview, clearReviewOutput\n   - Added DEFAULT_REVIEW_RUNNER_STATUS constant\n   - Added state variables for review runner\n   - Added message handlers for review:status, review:output, review:complete, review:error, review:cancelled\n   - Added handler functions: runReview, cancelReview, clearReviewOutput\n   - Updated return object with all new state/handlers\n\n7. **Type Error Fix**: Build failed because `review:cancelled` message type wasn't defined. I added `ReviewCancelledMessage` to types/index.ts and added it to ServerMessage union.\n\n8. **Dashboard Integration**:\n   - Added ReviewPanel import\n   - Added Sparkles icon import\n   - Destructured review runner state from useWebSocket\n   - Updated generateSubTab type to include 'quality'\n   - Added \"Quality Review\" tab to Generate section with ReviewPanel component\n\n9. **Git Work**:\n   - TypeScript and build passed\n   - Updated tasks.json to reflect actual completion\n   - Created commit with descriptive message\n   - Pushed to remote\n   - Created git tag v0.0.8\n\n10. **Stop Hook Feedback**: User provided feedback about \"PROMPT_ralph_phases_3-7.md\" - indicating there's additional work defined in that file.\n\n11. **Phase 3-7 Analysis**:\n    - Read PROMPT_ralph_phases_3-7.md and remaining.md\n    - Discovered these phases were separate from IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md tasks\n    - Phase 3: Testing (90% complete - missing CI workflow)\n    - Phase 4: Monitoring (95% complete - already integrated)\n    - Phase 5: Integrations (100% complete)\n    - Phase 6: Documentation (0% complete - no VitePress setup)\n    - Phase 7: Accessibility (85% complete)\n\n12. **Phase 3-7 Implementation Started**:\n    - Created .github/workflows/test.yml for CI\n    - Created docs/ VitePress structure\n    - Created docs/.vitepress/config.ts\n    - Created docs/index.md\n    - Created docs/getting-started/installation.md, quickstart.md, first-loop.md\n    - Created docs/user-guide/dashboard-overview.md, loop-modes.md, safety-controls.md\n    - Created docs/api/websocket-api.md\n    - Created docs/integrations/github.md\n\n13. **Where I Left Off**: I was in the middle of creating documentation files for Phase 6.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user asked me to implement functionality per specifications using IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, run validation, create tests as part of task scope, and commit changes. The main instruction was to verify all tasks in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md were complete before outputting ALL_TASKS_COMPLETE. After I outputted ALL_TASKS_COMPLETE, a stop hook provided feedback about \"PROMPT_ralph_phases_3-7.md\", indicating additional work was required beyond IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md tasks.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - React + TypeScript frontend with Express/WebSocket backend\n   - WebSocket message pattern: `domain:action` (e.g., `review:status`, `review:complete`)\n   - ReviewRunner (backend) for LLM-as-Judge quality reviews\n   - ReviewPanel (frontend component) for quality review UI\n   - useWebSocket hook pattern for state management\n   - Vitest for unit testing, Playwright for E2E testing\n   - VitePress for documentation\n   - GitHub Actions CI workflow\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **dashboard/src/hooks/useWebSocket.ts** - Core WebSocket hook for state management\n     - Added review runner types to imports:\n     ```typescript\n     import type { ..., ReviewRunnerStatus, ReviewConfig, ReviewResult } from '@/types';\n     ```\n     - Added interface properties:\n     ```typescript\n     // Review runner state (Feature Set 13 - LLM-as-Judge)\n     reviewRunnerStatus: ReviewRunnerStatus;\n     reviewRunnerOutput: string;\n     reviewRunnerResult: ReviewResult | null;\n     reviewRunnerError: string | null;\n     // Review runner handlers\n     runReview: (config: ReviewConfig) => void;\n     cancelReview: () => void;\n     clearReviewOutput: () => void;\n     ```\n     - Added default constant:\n     ```typescript\n     const DEFAULT_REVIEW_RUNNER_STATUS: ReviewRunnerStatus = {\n       running: false,\n       startedAt: null,\n     };\n     ```\n     - Added state variables:\n     ```typescript\n     const [reviewRunnerStatus, setReviewRunnerStatus] = useState<ReviewRunnerStatus>(DEFAULT_REVIEW_RUNNER_STATUS);\n     const [reviewRunnerOutput, setReviewRunnerOutput] = useState('');\n     const [reviewRunnerResult, setReviewRunnerResult] = useState<ReviewResult | null>(null);\n     const [reviewRunnerError, setReviewRunnerError] = useState<string | null>(null);\n     ```\n     - Added message handlers in switch statement:\n     ```typescript\n     case 'review:status':\n       setReviewRunnerStatus(message.payload);\n       if (message.payload.running) {\n         setReviewRunnerOutput('');\n         setReviewRunnerResult(null);\n         setReviewRunnerError(null);\n       }\n       break;\n     case 'review:output':\n       setReviewRunnerOutput((prev) => prev + message.payload.text);\n       break;\n     case 'review:complete':\n       setReviewRunnerResult(message.payload);\n       break;\n     case 'review:error':\n       setReviewRunnerError(message.payload.error);\n       break;\n     case 'review:cancelled':\n       setReviewRunnerStatus(DEFAULT_REVIEW_RUNNER_STATUS);\n       break;\n     ```\n     - Added handler functions:\n     ```typescript\n     const runReview = useCallback((config: ReviewConfig) => {\n       if (wsRef.current?.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {\n         wsRef.current.send(JSON.stringify({\n           type: 'review:run',\n           payload: config,\n         }));\n       }\n     }, []);\n\n     const cancelReview = useCallback(() => {\n       if (wsRef.current?.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {\n         wsRef.current.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'review:cancel' }));\n       }\n     }, []);\n\n     const clearReviewOutput = useCallback(() => {\n       setReviewRunnerOutput('');\n       setReviewRunnerResult(null);\n       setReviewRunnerError(null);\n     }, []);\n     ```\n\n   - **dashboard/src/types/index.ts** - Type definitions\n     - Added ReviewCancelledMessage:\n     ```typescript\n     export interface ReviewCancelledMessage ex